                         DMS Banner Stripper V2.0
                           Written by Lone Wolf
                          © 1992 - Latin Rascals
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Brief Documentation
-------------------

	Stripper removes ALL illegal tracks (ie Text Banners) from a DMS
File. Its usage is as follows:

	Stripper INFILE [OUTFILE]

	Outfile is optional, if none is specified the stripped DMS file
will overwrite the original file.

	If Outfile is not given, Stripper will write to a file in RAM:
called TEMPFILE.DMS which will be deleted after finishing its work.

Wildcarding
-----------

	I have included a script file which should do the work.
Stripper should be installed into your C: Directory, and the scriptfile
included (STRIP) should be installed into the S: Directory. Let's say you
have a directory in DH0: called Downloads, and would like to strip all
files ending with '.DMS'. In that case you would do:

	STRIP DH0:Downloads/#?.DMS

	Not much more to say, Good Luck!
